# pre-commit only lints the staged files. This is the gate that runs the checks
# which are cheap enough to wait on but too slow per-commit, so a push that
# would go red in CI fails here instead — about 40s on a warm cache.
#
# Deliberately not running the build: it roughly triples the wait and, unlike
# these two, has never failed on a tree where both of them passed. CI covers it.
npm run typecheck
npm test
